      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-293576",
      ":question/problem": "Company $A$ pays a modal starting salary of $$40000$ per year. The annual salaries of the currently advertised positions of Company $B$ are as follows:\n$$35000, $40000, $40000, $42000, $45000$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. The modal starting salary of Company $B$ is $$40000$.\n2. The modal starting salaries of the two companies are equal.\n3. A comparison of the modal salaries suggests that Company $A$ pays a greater starting salary than Company $B$."
